# f1 = add, f2 = called, f3 = the literal's getter, f4 = the descriptor's
# Where Link has proven who the getter in a slot is, compiled code calls that function without a test of the half. WHO IT IS was Link's word alone: the run time ended the process where a proven half was replaced or left its slot,
# but took any getter at the creation. Under a lie (an arm in which Link took the next function of the program for the getter) both kinds answered wrongly without a word as users build; only the checking lanes stopped.
# The run time holds the getter of every pair that goes into an accessor's slot against the TYPE of the field (RuntimeLayoutTable::accept(), tryDefineAbsentGetterInSlot(), tryDefineAccessorsOfLiteral()): the plan recorded none there.
# It records the closures of the proven function: another getter does not fit, and a proven half that cannot be laid ends the process: "StoreOfOtherType .. the compiler has proven that it never happens".
# RUN(ACCESSORS): link accesses mechanisms=all
# ACCESSORS: accessors L{{*}} getter=f3 proven
# ACCESSORS: accessors L{{*}} getter=f4 proven once-laid
# RUN(BORN): plan layouts mechanisms=all
# BORN: "add" {{*}}type=f3 accessor
# RUN(LAID): plan layouts mechanisms=all
# LAID: "add" appended {{*}}type=f4 accessor
